  "description": "The use of a skull symbol, universally associated with death or danger, to represent the emotional state of dread or exhaustion on Monday mornings may be perceived as potentially harmful due to its morbid imagery. While the intent is humorous and not targeted at any specific group, the visual metaphor may cause discomfort or be misinterpreted as threatening to viewers sensitive to death symbolism.",
